<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span><span id="S5.T1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RoboCasa main results.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Performance on RoboCasa.</span> <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.2 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ World2Act: Latent Action Post-Training via Skill-Compositional World Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a> summarizes our results. <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">World2Act</span> achieves a new state-of-the-art success rate on RoboCasa, notably outperforming established VLAs while requiring significantly less data. For instance, while UWM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite> utilizes <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> real demonstrations to achieve <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.8\%</annotation></semantics></math> success rate, Cosmos Policy+<span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">World2Act</span> reaches <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="66.3\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>66.3</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">66.3\%</annotation></semantics></math> using only <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> real demos and <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> imagined trajectories. While post-training GR00T-N1.6-ft with DreamGen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> yields a marginal <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.4\%</annotation></semantics></math> improvement, <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">World2Act</span> leverages the same 50 synthetic trajectory budget to achieve a substantial <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.5\%</annotation></semantics></math> gain, demonstrating higher data efficiency and more robust policy refinement capabilities.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S5.T2.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:73.9pt;vertical-align:-35.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-112.6pt,24.1pt) scale(0.605138551792603,0.605138551792603) ;">
<table id="S5.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
