<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S5.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LIBERO main results.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Performance on LIBERO.</span> <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ World2Act: Latent Action Post-Training via Skill-Compositional World Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 2</span></a> summarizes results on LIBERO across spatial, object, goal, and long-horizon skills. Overall, our post-training consistently strengthens the underlying policy and attains the top average performance among the compared methods. For GR00T-N1.6-ft, <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">World2Act</span> improves the base model from 97.0% to 98.1%, while DreamGen degrades performance to 92.6% (driven by failures on poor IDM pseudo-labeling action). On Cosmos Policy, <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">World2Act</span> also increases the performance by <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.T4.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:182.9pt;">
