<th id="S2.T2.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">-</th>
<th id="S2.T2.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">-</th>
<th id="S2.T2.3.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">0.701</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S2.T2.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">w/ LoRA (<math id="S2.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank=16</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">LoRA</td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">14.6 hrs</td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.714</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">w/ LoRA (<math id="S2.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank=32</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">LoRA</td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">15.3 hrs</td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.721</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.3.5" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F8F0;">
<th id="S2.T2.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.T2.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F8F0;">World2Act<span id="S2.T2.3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (Ours)</span></span></th>
<td id="S2.T2.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.T2.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F8F0;">Residual</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.T2.3.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F8F0;">6.8 hrs</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.3.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.T2.3.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F8F0;">0.726</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table S2</span>: </span><span id="S2.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Impact of adapter on GR00T-N1.6-ft+<span id="S2.T2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">World2Act</span>.<span id="S2.T2.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Comparison of our disjoint residual policy against standard LoRA adaptations on RoboCasa.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2a.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2a.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, <span id="S2a.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">World2Act</span> delivers stronger downstream manipulation performance, improving success by 0.5% over LoRA (<math id="S2a.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank=32</annotation></semantics></math>). As illustrated in Fig. 4 of the main paper, our residual policy uses action adapters specifically designed to leverage the pre-aligned, shared latent space of video-action modalities. LoRA, conversely, initializes low-rank matrices from scratch and optimizes them within intermediate layers, which limits its capacity to exploit the rich, pre-structured multimodal knowledge acquired during Stage 1 pretraining.</p>
</div>
